  "Question": "What is the area, in square centimeters, of a circle with a radius of 10 cm? Use \\(314/100\\) for pi.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "314",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A circle's area is \\(\\pi\\) times the radius multiplied by itself. Using \\(3.14\\) for \\(\\pi\\),\n\\[\n3.14\\times(10\\times10)=3.14\\times100=314.\n\\]\nThe area is approximately \\(314\\text{ cm}^2\\).",
